/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "=+\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487078} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae07e5e5-6e19-529b-9f50-bceccec9dd57" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e871b676-2c06-50d7-81b0-8662a3a9169b" :question/math-academy-id "q-253041" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=[0,\\infty ).$ Complete the following reasoning to determine $inf(A)$ and $sup(A).$\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A,$ and the supremum is the {{field-2}} of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ is {{field-3}}, we have $inf(A)$ {{field-4}}.\n\nSince $A$ is {{field-5}}, we have $sup(A)$ {{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A,$ and the supremum is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le 0$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,0]$ contains only lower bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>0$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>0.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,0]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,0]=0.\n$$\n\nNext, to find the supremum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSince $A$ is unbounded above, $A$ has no upper bounds, and $sup(A)=+\\infty .$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of a set $A$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ of $A,$ and the supremum is the $\\text{smallest upper bound}$ of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ is $\\text{bounded below},$ we have $inf(A)=0.$\n\nSince $A$ is $\\text{unbounded above},$ we have $sup(A)=+\\infty .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162157 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fee0e08c-5a7a-5f78-83aa-39679bb3b17b" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff25cbe-96b0-5244-b7a8-2ae819809b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "smallest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160497} {:answer/id #uuid "bf49f765-e10d-5efa-8f02-23884631cbb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160498} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a32217-222b-5694-b0e5-e9eef314a757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160499} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b61bea-0d92-5db0-8f02-d0fdb50f01f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "smallest upper bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8a32217-222b-5694-b0e5-e9eef314a757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "greatest lower bound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160499} :answer-field/id #uuid "b88ee89b-b237-5608-b215-04a9aa8e8677" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1881584d-67a8-5364-9525-db8912138dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486644} {:answer/id #uuid "4a30385b-0a6e-5893-a6d2-8df76ccd6427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.t