th} :answer/value "inf(A)=0\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487058} :answer-field/id #uuid "da62234a-a027-5829-82b2-366ee9d80a0b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183c7bd1-c965-51f8-b1ac-7a7863aba7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486643} {:answer/id #uuid "1930fe5c-7248-5f8e-9be2-f6fdc0db788e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183c7bd1-c965-51f8-b1ac-7a7863aba7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486643} :answer-field/id #uuid "fadb4645-7f64-5b96-9f43-b05796106137" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6094a958-deb9-5dcb-b85d-1d2a1044d120" :question/math-academy-id "q-253511" :question/problem "Consider the set $A=[0,2].$ Complete the following reasoning to identify $inf(A).$\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the {{field-1}} of $A.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x{{field-2}}{{field-3}}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- Any number in the set $x\\le 0$ is smaller than or equal to the elements of $A.$ Thus, the set $(-\\infty ,0]$ contains only lower bounds of $A.$\n\n- Any number in the set $x>0$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $x$ for any $x>0.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,0]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,0]=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $0$ is also the minimum of $A.$\n\nThe completed reasoning is given below.\n\nThe infimum of $A$ is the $\\text{greatest lower bound}$ bound of $A.$\n\nThe set of lower bounds of $A$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{x\\in R\\,:\\,x\\le 0\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $inf(A)=0\\in A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe2b2c0-23a0-5bd0-8bc7-c12139820b61" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f73ae8d-f2e8-5cf5-bf54-d34ec79a90c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=3\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486690} {:answer/id #uuid "34e09dab-11a6-5462-9d88-bddc2bd9213b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$inf(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486707} {:answer/id #uuid "42fc1632-c9c1-5009-88f7-185a50c722d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=3\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486738} {:answer/id #uuid "c019112a-3b1b-5e5d-bb33-cb7e429db013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487019} {:answer/id #uuid "f49f1a1a-8ba9-5ac6-a28d-df18540cdfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c019112a-3b1b-5e5d-bb33-cb7e429db013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487019} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d4e4ded-e058-51a6-b1cd-e47d3c47538e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13b42a92-bc61-5733-b661-85ce69e84b97" :question/math-academy-id "q-253513" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{3-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=3-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/35/351e7bb3db6811be2a690fbd3fc2dc99282c4ff676e9116717d85515a298cf80.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is increasing and converges to $3.$ The minimum of $A$ is \n\n$$\nmin(A)={a}_{1}=3-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{1}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $x\\le {a}_{1}$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $x>{a}_{1}$ cannot be a lower bound because ${a}_{1},$ an element of $A,$ is smaller than $x.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{2}]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{2}]=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\frac{5}{2}$ is the minimum of $A.$ Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ninf(A)=\\frac{5}{2}\\in A.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162158 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe2b2c0-23a0-5bd0-8bc7-c12139820b61" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa61d86-b0f9-5a61-a276-87b1e8131516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{3}\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486655} {:answer/id #uuid "31002c35-5985-5fde-b87e-39583a093fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{3}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486696} {:answer/id #uuid "7e78293d-aec3-58b5-a329-6318d6d9600d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$inf(A)$ does not exist" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486867} {:answer/id #uuid "800778ee-d630-5816-9df2-7a05075e38f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=2\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486873} {:answer/id #uuid "95715de7-9216-56ef-b8bf-3a456d9858be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=2\\notin A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31002c35-5985-5fde-b87e-39583a093fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "inf(A)=\\frac{5}{3}\\in A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486696} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec0ca0f3-190b-55df-a54b-77392ca10b39" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4eaf9cf-b8c1-5f93-bf45-1dc2cc8b5b67" :question/math-academy-id "q-253525" :question/problem "Consider the following set.\n\n$$\nA=\\{2-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nFor this set, we have that {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The infimum of $A$ is the greatest lower bound of $A.$\n\nTo find the infimum of this set, we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nThe elements of $A$ are the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n},\\,n\\in N=\\{1,2,3,4,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's draw some points of our sequence on the real line:\n\n![](images/72/72fa47f25042b5187a87262b23e0976429909011b1516bc6018e70cd4f881f11.png)\n\nWe see that ${a}_{n}$ is increasing and converges to $5.$ The minimum of $A$ is \n\n$$\nmin(A)={a}_{1}=2-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $x\\le {a}_{1}$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $x>{a}_{1}$ cannot be a lower bound because ${a}_{1},$ an element of $A,$ is smaller than $x.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{3}]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and \n\n$$\ninf(A)=max(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{3}]=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\frac{5}{3}$ is the minimum of $A.$ Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ninf(A)=\\frac{5}{3}\\in A.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162156 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f950f3da-81c2-574a-b7f7-06d88945c249" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "089cddaa-aa6b-5dcb-bd04-ae36f98a9046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "089cddaa-aa6b-5dcb-bd04-ae36f98a9046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486611} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0beefd6-38b7-58b0-b684-3936a2521ce3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "546541ff-37d6-5bb0-b37e-29f5b9d47681" :question/math-academy-id "q-253541" :question/problem "What is the infimum of the set $B=\\{-0.15,\\,-0.2,\\,0.05,\\,0,\\,9\\}?$\n\n$inf(B)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The infimum of a set $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B.$\n\nIf $B$ is a finite set, the infimum of $B$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}inf(B) & =min\\{-0.15,\\,-0.2,\\,0.05,\\,0,\\,9\\}=-0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162156 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f950f3da-81c2-574a-b7f7-06d88945c249" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44beebbd-07c2-5851-ba19-b05775c541e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44beebbd-07c2-5851-ba19-b05775c541e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486743} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e05f0be-24c8-5b6d-94b7-cae94e3dae5b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df0bc2ee-bd6a-5b2e-965b-ef9ca16078ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-253543" :question/problem "What is the supremum of the set $B=\\{-5,\\,4,\\,1,\\,0,\\,-3\\}?$\n\n$sup(B)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $B$ is the smallest upper bound of $B.$\n\nIf $B$ is a finite set, the supremum of $B$ equals its maximum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(B) & =max\\{-5,\\,4,\\,1,\\,0,\\,-3\\}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162156 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f950f3da-81c2-574a-b7f7-06d88945c249" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of a Finite Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a10166f-357f-5f79-8588-8f1e9cacb997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a10166f-357f-5f79-8588-8f1e9cacb997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486824} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df0afb2-d916-50c2-9c1a-18d1e73450fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d279c4a-988e-5c29-a6a0-5c2bb436ded0" :question/math-academy-id "q-253550" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\frac{1}{5-n}:n\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the supremum of $A?$\n\n$sup(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. \n\nFirst, let's write down all the terms of our set by substituting $n=1,2,3,4$ into the expression for the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5-0} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-1} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-3} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5-4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1\\}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162157 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fee0e08c-5a7a-5f78-83aa-39679bb3b17b" :knowledge-point/title "Supremum and Infimum of an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi